Where the credit appears in this repository:

  src/data/template.js      what the running app reads it from
  src/App.jsx               the line at the foot of the sidebar
  src/components/Landing.jsx   the credit in the landing page footer
  index.html                <meta name="generator">, <meta name="attribution">
  index.html                JSON-LD, a schema.org SoftwareApplication node
  scripts/generate-seo.js   what robots.txt and humans.txt are written from
  NOTICE                    this file, copied into the build and served
  README.md                 the Credits section

scripts/generate-seo.js fails the build if the generator tag, the attribution
tag or the author's name has gone missing from dist/index.html. That check is
not obfuscation and it is not meant to be unbeatable: anyone who owns a fork
can take all of it out. It is spread across enough files that removing it is
a deliberate act, visible in the diff, rather than something a refactor does
by accident.
